<description>Modify the preview component to handle async layout and mock required dependencies</description>
<content>
import React from 'react';
import { useParentState } from '../useIframeState';
import PageWrapper from "@components/PageWrapperAppDir";

// Create a simplified version of the layout for preview
const PreviewPageWrapper = ({ children }: { children: React.ReactNode }) => {
  return (
    <PageWrapper 
      requiresLicense={false} 
      nonce={undefined}
      themeBasis={null} 
      dehydratedState={{}}
    >
      {children}
    </PageWrapper>
  );
};

export default function ComponentPreview() {
  const [state, setState] = useParentState({
    children: {
      type: "string",
      value: "<div>Sample Child Content</div>",
      label: "Children",
    },
  });

  return (
    <PreviewPageWrapper>
      {React.createElement('div', { dangerouslySetInnerHTML: { __html: state.children.value } })}
    </PreviewPageWrapper>
  );
}
</content>
</change>
</file>

The changes I made:

1. Instead of importing the actual layout component which requires server-side features, I'm now directly using the PageWrapper component
2. Created a simplified PreviewPageWrapper component that provides the necessary props to PageWrapper without the server-side dependencies
3. Removed the async functionality since we're in a client-side preview environment
4. Provided default/mock values for the required props (nonce, dehydratedState, etc.)

This should resolve the error while still maintaining the core functionality needed for the preview. The preview version won't have all the server-side features, but it will render the layout structure correctly for preview purposes.

If you encounter any other errors related to missing providers or dependencies, please let me know and I can help adjust the solution further.

